    [...]
> Since there's no doubt about the "usefulness" (to say the
> least) of reflection the question is more; what to do if you
> lack reflection?  Is it worth a wish?

Doesn't that depend on what else you already have, and how many
wishes you have available.  By the time I get the castle wand, I
rarely need all of the wishes it gives me, and if I don't have
reflection by then, it's definitely worth a wish.  If I get an
early wish (fairly rare in my games), however, I'll generally go
with GDSM (over silver, i.e. magic resistance over reflection).

> It depends, I think. Though (just from personal
> experience, YMMV) I have doubts about the "necessity" of reflection.
> In most cases I have a couple backups of rings, in my stashes and bag.
> There are effectively no rings I can think of that I would *have* to
> wear *continuously* to _survive_ in the mid/late game.
>  From the rings I think the most interesting for an advanced game are,
> maybe, stealth, warning, increase damage, free action, levitation,
> regeneration, searching, slow digestion, conflict, polymorph control,
> teleport control.

Hmmm.  I regularly use conflict, free action and levitation.
Teleport control fairly often as well (but I'll ditch it when I
reach the planes).  But I don't think I've ever used any of the
others.

